**Root cause:** `login()` calls `.id` on whatever `getUser()` returns without checking it exists. When a session has no `user` (e.g. an unauthenticated visitor hitting the login page), `getUser` returns `undefined`, and `user.id` throws exactly `TypeError: cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')`.

**Fix:** guard in `login()` — if there's no user, return `undefined`/`null` instead of dereferencing `.id`, so the login page can render a "not logged in" state instead of crashing.

**Risk:** low — this is the entire repo, there are no other callers to break.

